{title: O My Son Absalom}
{subtitle: 2 Samuel 19:1}
{key: Cm}
{tempo: 126}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Cm] | [Cm] | [Cm] |
| [Cm] | [Cm] | [Fm] | [Fm] | ×2
| [Cm] | [Cm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Good news for my lord the king
The [Fm]Lord has delivered you today
[Cm]Is it well with the young man Absa[Fm]lom
May all your [Cm]enemies be like that [Fm]young man
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
O my [Cm]son Absalom
My [Fm]son, my son Absa[Cm]lom
[Fm]Would I had died in[Cm]stead of you
[Fm]O Absalom, my son, my [Cm]son
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Cm] | [Cm] | [Fm] | [Fm] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Cm]The king was deeply moved
He went [Fm]up to the chamber over the gate and [Cm]wept
And as he [Fm]went, he said
O my [Cm]son
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [Cm] | [Cm] | [Fm] | [Fm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Cm]The victory that day was turned to mourn[Fm]ing
[Cm]The people stole into the c[Fm]ity
[Cm]As people steal in who are as[Fm]hamed
The king [Cm]covered his face and cried with a [Fm]loud voice
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Outro}
| [Cm] | [Cm] | [Fm] | [Fm] | ×2
| [Fm] |
